## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10) | **Calibration:** Integration (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch executes per run. If the type is always `User`, the `PremiumUser` path is never tested—a hidden gap.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — one code path is silently untested.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** 3-second hard-coded sleep. Non-deterministic (may fail on slow CI), inflates suite runtime. Even in integration tests, polling/event-driven waits are superior.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of fixed sleep
    var notified = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(notified, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk:** Flaky failures in CI; slow feedback loop (3s per invocation).

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← no assertion
```

**Problem:** Passes as long as no exception is thrown. A bug that silently drops inserts would go undetected.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk:** False-pass — coverage looks good but nothing is verified.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Smell)

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);          // no message
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);   // no message
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email); // no message
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);      // no message
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions, zero diagnostic messages. A failure in CI reports only "Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>" with no context about *which property* was being checked or *why* it matters.

**Fix:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist unchanged.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist unchanged.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be a positive integer.");
```

**Risk:** Slower debugging when tests fail remotely.

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written Tests)

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Minimal, targeted assertion (`Assert.IsNull`) |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion (3) is self-documenting after adding 3 items |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async pattern, meaningful assertion |

The fixture design is also sound: in-memory SQLite avoids true Mystery Guest issues, and `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` properly isolate each test.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Split into two focused test methods |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling helper |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Add message parameters to assertions |

Fixes 1–3 directly prevent false-passes or flakiness. Fix 4 is a maintainability improvement for CI debugging.
